### Password requirements

- Never store plaintext passwords.
- Never store reversible passwords.
- Never hardcode passwords in JavaScript.
- Use a password-hashing algorithm appropriate to the browser environment.
- Prefer Argon2id when a properly maintained offline implementation is available.
- If using native Web Crypto only, use PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 with a unique random salt and an appropriately calibrated work factor.
- Version password-hashing parameters to support future upgrades.
- Never silently downgrade password security.

Clearly distinguish offline authentication from online identity verification.

Do not claim that offline authentication can independently verify an administrator through an external authority when internet connectivity is unavailable.

